  "body": "I'm not sure if this is the right repo, or if I should be posting somewhere CORS-specifc. \r\n\r\nI'm also not familiar with all the history/rationale behind the current list of CORS simple response headers, so consider this a question as much as a suggestion.\r\n\r\nBut: would it make sense to have `Link` as a simple response header? I don't immediately see a security risk here, and I imagine any server sending a Link would want this data to be usable by browser clients.",
